---
description: Core coding standards for the whole repo
alwaysApply: true
---
- TypeScript `strict: true`, no `any` (use `unknown` + narrowing), no non-null `!` unless justified in a comment.
- Prefer named exports. One component per file. Files: `PascalCase.tsx` for components, `useCamelCase.ts` hooks, `camelCase.ts` utils/services.
- Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only for interactivity/animation.
- Validate external data (Firestore, forms, env) with zod schemas in `src/lib/schemas`.
- No dead code, no commented-out code, no console.log in committed code.
- Env/config via `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_*` read only in `src/lib/env.ts`.
- Small, focused commits; conventional commit messages (`feat:`, `chore:`, `test:`, `fix:`, `docs:`).
- Content rules (AGENTS.md #4) are hard constraints — also for seed data and placeholders.
